`Schedule A1, Part A — the retirement age in months of a woman born in month` `the month` `of` `the year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `born` AT MOST `the month count of` 6  `of` 1944 THEN 720   -- to June 1944: 60
        IF `born` AT MOST `the month count of` 8  `of` 1944 THEN 724   -- July and August 1944: 60 and 4 months
        IF `born` AT MOST `the month count of` 4  `of` 1945 THEN 728   -- September 1944 to April 1945: 60 and 8 months
        IF `born` AT MOST `the month count of` 12 `of` 1945 THEN 732   -- May to December 1945: 61
        IF `born` AT MOST `the month count of` 8  `of` 1946 THEN 736   -- January to August 1946: 61 and 4 months
        IF `born` AT MOST `the month count of` 4  `of` 1947 THEN 740   -- September 1946 to April 1947: 61 and 8 months
        IF `born` AT MOST `the month count of` 12 `of` 1955 THEN 744   -- May 1947 to December 1955: 62
        OTHERWISE                                      REFUSE "Part A of Schedule A1 gives no row for a woman born in 1956 or later: section 1 sends her to the Retirement Age Law"
    WHERE `born` MEANS `the month count of` `the month` `of` `the year`

@ref NII Schedule A1, Part A, women, lines 4385-4396
