§§ `The day a person reaches an age`

-- A person reaches an age of N months on the day N months after the date of birth. Where the later
-- month has that day of the month it is that day, under every reading. Where it lacks it, the text does
-- not say which day it is (the ambiguity of row IL-08's fork N4, inventory item DATE). The three
-- readings are kept by name (nouns); RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG): declined by default, and
-- declined only on the days on which the readings give different answers to "has she reached it".
@ref NII Schedule A1 (an age in years and months, no day); Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `A reading of the day an age is reached where the later month lacks the day of birth`
`the reading this row takes where the day an age is reached does not exist` MEANS
    `age: such a day is declined`

@ref NII Schedule A1; the ruling above
GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the age in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day a person born on` `the date of birth` `reaches the age in months` `the age in months` `, the last day of a shorter month` MEANS
    `add months` `the date of birth` `the age in months`

@ref NII Schedule A1; the ruling above
GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the age in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day a person born on` `the date of birth` `reaches the age in months` `the age in months` `, the 1st of the next month` MEANS
    IF   DATE_DAY clamped EQUALS DATE_DAY `the date of birth`
    THEN clamped
    ELSE `add months` (YMD (DATE_YEAR clamped) (DATE_MONTH clamped) 1) 1
    WHERE clamped MEANS `add months` `the date of birth` `the age in months`

@ref NII Schedule A1; the ruling above
GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the age in months` IS A NUMBER
      `the day`           IS A DATE
      r                   IS A `A reading of the day an age is reached where the later month lacks the day of birth`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person born on` `the date of birth` `has reached the age in months` `the age in months` `on` `the day` `, reading` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `age: the last day of the shorter month` THEN byClamp
    WHEN `age: the 1st of the next month`         THEN byRoll
    WHEN `age: such a day is declined`            THEN
        IF   byClamp EQUALS byRoll
        THEN byClamp
        ELSE REFUSE "the Schedule fixes an age in years and months and does not say which day a person reaches it where the month she reaches it in lacks her day of birth"
    WHERE
        byClamp MEANS `the day` AT LEAST `the day a person born on` `the date of birth` `reaches the age in months` `the age in months` `, the last day of a shorter month`
        byRoll  MEANS `the day` AT LEAST `the day a person born on` `the date of birth` `reaches the age in months` `the age in months` `, the 1st of the next month`

@ref NII Schedule A1; the ruling above
GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the age in months` IS A NUMBER
      `the day`           IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person born on` `the date of birth` `has reached the age in months` `the age in months` `on` `the day` MEANS
    `a person born on` `the date of birth` `has reached the age in months` `the age in months` `on` `the day`
        `, reading` `the reading this row takes where the day an age is reached does not exist`

§§ `s 1 "גיל הפרישה" — the retirement age of a person`

-- (1) for a man, Part A (men) by his month of birth; (2) for a woman, Part A (women) by her month of birth, and
-- "if she was born in 1956 or later, the age fixed for her in accordance with the Retirement Age Law, 5764-2004".
-- That Law is deposited and row IL-27 encodes it (retirement-age-law.l4, vendored unchanged); the wrapper
-- `nii-s1-retirement-age-law.l4` takes the month and year of birth. s 3 of the Law fixes 67 for a man and 65 for a
-- woman, and s 6 and Parts A and B of its Schedule give the ages of those born up to April 1942 (men) and December
-- 1969 (women). A man's age is Part A of this Schedule, as s 1 (1) says, and the Law's age for a man is the same
-- (the tests compare them); the Law has a gap for a woman born before May 1947, who is not asked here, her age
-- being Part A of this Schedule.
@ref NII s 1 "גיל הפרישה", lines 130-132; Schedule A1, Part A; Retirement Age Law ss 3, 6, Part B
GIVEN p IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 1 — the retirement age in months of` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p's sex
    WHEN `male`   THEN `Schedule A1, Part A — the retirement age in months of a man born on` (p's `date of birth`)
    WHEN `female` THEN
        IF   DATE_YEAR (p's `date of birth`) LESS THAN 1956
        THEN `Schedule A1, Part A — the retirement age in months of a woman born on` (p's `date of birth`)
        ELSE `the Retirement Age Law's retirement age in months of a woman born in month` (DATE_MONTH (p's `date of birth`)) `of` (DATE_YEAR (p's `date of birth`))

@ref NII s 1 "גיל הפרישה"; the ruling above
GIVEN p   IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      rd  IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 — the retirement age is reached by` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd MEANS
    `a person born on` (p's `date of birth`) `has reached the age in months` (`s 1 — the retirement age in months of` p) `on` `the day` `, reading` (rd's `the day an age is reached`)

@ref NII s 1 "גיל הפרישה"; the ruling above
GIVEN p   IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 — the retirement age is reached by` p `on` `the day` MEANS
    `s 1 — the retirement age is reached by` p `on` `the day` `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
